# Agent contract

Repository: qoptics-inference-bench. Package: `qoinfer`. Owner: Yuedong Sun
(`@YueDongSun`) writes the science. Agents write engineering that traces to
`spec/` or an ADR in `docs/adr/`.

Read `AGENTS.md` before editing. `CLAUDE.md` points at the same file.

`example_000_smoke` is a format demo, not science. Do not invent physics,
units, tolerances, conventions, or literature values. If `spec/` does not
state a fact, open a GitHub issue labelled `needs-science-decision`, quote
the exact line, list the options, and stop that piece of work.

Comments, docs, ADRs, and instructions are English. snake_case for
project-owned paths and identifiers. Keep required external names
(`AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `Dockerfile`, `pyproject.toml`, `task.toml`,
`.pre-commit-config.yaml`, `.cursor/`, `.claude/`, GitHub template names).

No attribution trailers on ordinary commits. One agent owns one issue,
branch, and worktree. Do not touch another agent's branch. Do not
force-remove worktrees or branches.

Preparation, installation, registration, a successful call, and end-to-end
acceptance are separate states. A pull request names the state of each claim
and pastes the command output for anything it calls verified.

Never commit credentials, host inventories, chat histories, tokens, or
token-bearing URLs. Repository visibility is the owner's decision.
Update README and affected docs only with behaviour verified in that PR.
